    <h2>4. Review and Removal Process</h2>

    <p>
      Upon receiving a valid copyright complaint, we will review the notice and
      may remove or disable access to the allegedly infringing material where
      appropriate.
    </p>

    <p>
      We reserve the right to request additional information before taking
      action and to reject incomplete, fraudulent, or abusive notices.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Counter-Notification</h2>

    <p>
      If you believe that material removed or disabled as a result of a
      copyright complaint was removed in error or misidentification, you may
      submit a counter-notification containing sufficient information supporting
      your claim.
    </p>

    <p>
      Upon receipt of a valid counter-notification, we may restore the material
      in accordance with applicable laws unless the original complainant
      initiates legal proceedings.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Repeat Infringers</h2>

    <p>
      Anikawa reserves the right to restrict, suspend, or terminate access for
      users who are determined to be repeat copyright infringers, where
      applicable.
    </p>

    <h2>7. False Claims</h2>

    <p>
      Submitting false, misleading, or fraudulent copyright complaints or
      counter-notifications may result in legal liability under applicable laws.
      Please ensure that all notices are truthful and submitted in good faith.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Changes to This Policy</h2>

